      "abstract": "<jats:title>Abstract</jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>Smart Grid-IoT powered energy systems have been quick to adopt renewable sources, and this has not only led to a change in how energy is generated and distributed but also to the distribution of more environmentally friendly, reliable, and locally managed solutions. Currently, the intrusion detection in the Smart Grid–IoT research suffers from many problems. Most of them have low accuracy when dealing with high dimensionality data of the Smart Grid–IoT environment. These issues lead to difficulties in managing temporally correlated data and, moreover, the current approach is not capable of real-time processing and does not easily adapt to new attack patterns. To put it simply, not only a majority of the security issues require the creation of an effective, scalable, and intelligent security framework but they also require the protection of cyber-physical systems for the modern renewable energy ones. This paper proposes a Reformer Integrated Variational Architecture (RIVA) integrated with Crested Stride Tuning and Estimation Principle (C-STEP) for ensuring security and robustness in smart grid - IoT systems. RIVA is an attention transformer sequentially built upon the variational auto encoder basis that operates severely on the dependencies of spatiotemporal data streams of IoT and Smart Grid. The performance of the proposed work is validated using the Gotham-2025, SWaT, CICIDS 2017 datasets, and the results stated that the model gets 0.99 scores for accuracy, precision, recall, and F1 when compared to other transformer, hybrid, and conventional deep learning approaches practically without exceptions which clearly it outperforms them.</jats:p>",
